{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1210364-lunars-entering-the-underworld","id":1210364,"title":"Lunars entering the Underworld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-23T04:41:44-07:00","id":1210364,"title":"Lunars entering the Underworld","content":"I'm running an Exalted 2nd edition campaign in which two Abyssals have &quot;befriended&quot; two Lunars who were betrayed by their pack. How would the Lunars be able to get into the Underworld along with the Abyssals? Would they have to go through a shadowland or is there a charm that would let them bypass that? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T04:55:25-07:00","id":1210368,"title":"","content":"Afaik there are no charms for this (outside of that one necromancy spell)<br /> <br /> But nothing prevents The Wyld from &quot;randomly&quot; creating a (portable) passageway that the Lunars can stabilise with Ritual of Lunar Stability; like a door that can be picked up and carried and opens onto the underworld, or a blanket of night that allows the bearer to treat shadowlands as being &quot;at night&quot; 24/7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T06:31:45-07:00","id":1210386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucardtes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1210364-lunars-entering-the-underworld#post1210364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running an Exalted 2nd edition campaign in which two Abyssals have &amp;quot;befriended&amp;quot; two Lunars who were betrayed by their pack. How would the Lunars be able to get into the Underworld along with the Abyssals? Would they have to go through a shadowland or is there a charm that would let them bypass that? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Exalted can walk in and out if the Underworld as easily as anyone else, and anyone else can walk in and out as easily as Abyssals... barring Abyssal Charms or powerful Necromancy.<br /> <br /> Lunars don\u2019t need anything more than to walk into whatever Shadowland the Abyssals are presumably using.<br /> <br /> If the Abyssals are using a Charm or Spell, then it can probably transport passengers. They might be able to help the Lunars as means to construct a sorcerous portal, assuming the Abyssal necromancer doesn\u2019t build such a portal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T07:33:48-07:00","id":1210409,"title":"","content":"As Sunder the Gold said, nothing fancy required - &quot;just&quot; a shadowland. And while the popular imagination goes to large Deathlord ruled domains, remember there are all kinds of Shadowlands throughout the map. If I remember...<ul><li><b>The Blessed Isle - </b>despite being a bastion of stability, I remember there being a cave (hidden or long avoided) where some slaughter took place - so going deep enough, you can find yourself exiting into Stygia or the Labyrinthe</li> <li><b>Slain Primordials</b> (and/or Behemoths) often created Shadowlands where they fell.</li> <li><b>Large Slaughters</b> (especially with little chance of burial or &quot;recycling&quot; seem to fit). Battlefields where bodies aren't buried work - animals eating a village of humans <i>probably</i> doesn't work - predators hunting humans for giggles (creating a lifeless copse in the forest) <i>probably would</i>.</li> <li><b>The Wyld?</b> I can't recall where I get this impression (I know Celestial Directions - Wyld - mentions ghosts going to explore the Wyld.. but I don't have my book with me). It poses all kinds of neat questions (in terms of celestial geography).</li> <li><b>Deathlord Domains</b> - not all deathlords are hostile. One of my old characters was a <i>Abyssal-friendly Lunar</i>.<ul><li>Her settlement/outpost was often attacked by barbarians &amp; beastmen - and she Exalted during one of those raids - <i>therefore</i> she refused anything related to &quot;barbarians, beastmen&quot; (and the Silver Pact by extension).</li> <li>The game was set in the North - and the Lover Clad was only a few hundred miles from the &quot;main city&quot; - and it turned out her bio says she tries to recruit Exalts (she has Solars &amp; Terrestrials serving her - and was open to Lunars &amp; Sidereals). When gameplay began, I bumped into a few other players who <i>also</i> favored the Lover Clad, so we made a mixed circle.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Necromancy</b> - the obvious option everyone mentioned.</li> </ul><b>Glories of Luna - and Ink Monkeys </b>- are your best choices for <b>death-related Lunar charms</b>. They play up more of the &quot;world walker&quot; theme, with powers that are &quot;death-ish&quot; (animating a corpse into a psuedo-zombie via parasitic worms; spitting out wasps; creating a shield-arm of bone; etc) or death-friendly (one of which extends the &quot;Wyld-navigation&quot; charm to apply to other realms of existence... so now you can travel the Labyrinthe or Malfeas with the same ease you do the Wyld).<br /> <br /> Lastly, while most players think of <i>scavengers</i> (animals that eat the dead) - there's another category of animals that <i>pretend to be dead </i>(fish who discolor themselves to attract corpse-hunting scavengers and then <i>eat </i>the scavengers; snakes who bleed from eyes &amp; mouth to feign sickness &amp; death) as well as animals that <i>injure themselves</i> (newts that stab their own ribs through their skin to create ridges as self-defense.....the newts heal the wounds later rather quickly; frogs that snap their own toe-bones through the flesh to create stub-claws..... less &quot;wolverine&quot;, more &quot;zombie fingers clawing you&quot;). Plus there are horse-sized maggots (around Thorns), hippo-sized centipedes (beneath Gethamane) and other horrific critters. <b>Any</b> of these animals could be useful to Lunars traveling and hiding among the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T13:27:28-07:00","id":1210570,"title":"","content":"Well, since we are speaking 1e....<br /> <br /> 1 - Get a knack to add ghosts to one's library of forms.<br /> 2 - Turn into the ghost consumed.<br /> 3 - Enter the Underworld by simply dematerializing.<br /> 4 - <i>Profit.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}